$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Health Communication/Week 08/Applied decision

::HC-W8-037::In Week 8 (Digital Health and Social Media Communication), in a youth-friendly service, a team immediately chooses Instagram before defining the audience or objective. What is the BEST correction? {
=Diagnose the communication problem and audience before selecting a channel#Correct. Channel choice should follow the communication problem, audience and objective.
~Increase posting frequency#Not the best answer. Channel choice should follow the communication problem, audience and objective.
~Use more technical terminology#Not the best answer. Channel choice should follow the communication problem, audience and objective.
~Remove all audience feedback#Not the best answer. Channel choice should follow the communication problem, audience and objective.
}

::HC-W8-038::In Week 8 (Digital Health and Social Media Communication), in a rural health centre, a programme reports success only because many people saw its content. What is the strongest critique? {
=Exposure is an implementation measure and does not by itself prove understanding or behaviour change#Correct. Reach matters, but it sits earlier in the pathway than comprehension, action or health outcomes.
~High reach proves the health outcome improved#Not the best answer. Reach matters, but it sits earlier in the pathway than comprehension, action or health outcomes.
~Reach and behaviour are the same measure#Not the best answer. Reach matters, but it sits earlier in the pathway than comprehension, action or health outcomes.
~The programme should stop measuring exposure#Not the best answer. Reach matters, but it sits earlier in the pathway than comprehension, action or health outcomes.
}

::HC-W8-039::In Week 8 (Digital Health and Social Media Communication), in an urban community clinic, a message is scientifically accurate but the intended audience cannot act because the service is unavailable. What is the best interpretation? {
=The communication may be accurate but is not operationally actionable#Correct. Actionability requires a feasible pathway to the recommended behaviour.
~The audience lacks motivation by definition#Not the best answer. Actionability requires a feasible pathway to the recommended behaviour.
~More repetition will solve the service barrier#Not the best answer. Actionability requires a feasible pathway to the recommended behaviour.
~Accuracy automatically makes the intervention effective#Not the best answer. Actionability requires a feasible pathway to the recommended behaviour.
}

::HC-W8-040::In Week 8 (Digital Health and Social Media Communication), in a national public-health campaign, community members repeatedly raise the same concern, but the programme never records or responds to it. Which system is most clearly missing? {
=A feedback and adaptation loop#Correct. Listening only creates value when insight is documented, acted on where appropriate, and reported back.
~A larger logo#Not the best answer. Listening only creates value when insight is documented, acted on where appropriate, and reported back.
~A longer technical report#Not the best answer. Listening only creates value when insight is documented, acted on where appropriate, and reported back.
~A higher advertising budget#Not the best answer. Listening only creates value when insight is documented, acted on where appropriate, and reported back.
}

::HC-W8-041::In Week 8 (Digital Health and Social Media Communication), in a district vaccination programme, a campaign uses a striking statistic with no denominator or baseline. What is the main communication risk? {
=The audience may misinterpret the magnitude of risk or effect#Correct. Risk information needs context, denominators and appropriate framing.
~The message will always be too long#Not the best answer. Risk information needs context, denominators and appropriate framing.
~Denominators are irrelevant in communication#Not the best answer. Risk information needs context, denominators and appropriate framing.
~The source becomes automatically credible#Not the best answer. Risk information needs context, denominators and appropriate framing.
}

::HC-W8-042::In Week 8 (Digital Health and Social Media Communication), in a maternal-health campaign, a team labels non-adoption as “ignorance” without studying access, norms or service barriers. What should happen first? {
=Conduct formative diagnosis of behavioural and communication determinants#Correct. Audience and behavioural diagnosis should precede message selection.
~Design a harsher slogan#Not the best answer. Audience and behavioural diagnosis should precede message selection.
~Increase fear immediately#Not the best answer. Audience and behavioural diagnosis should precede message selection.
~Assume knowledge is the only determinant#Not the best answer. Audience and behavioural diagnosis should precede message selection.
}

::HC-W8-043::In Week 8 (Digital Health and Social Media Communication), in an HIV prevention programme, an organisation changes guidance when new evidence arrives but tries to hide the earlier advice. What would better protect trust? {
=Explain what changed, why it changed, and what people should do now#Correct. Transparent updates can preserve credibility when evidence evolves.
~Delete all previous communication without explanation#Not the best answer. Transparent updates can preserve credibility when evidence evolves.
~Claim the guidance never changed#Not the best answer. Transparent updates can preserve credibility when evidence evolves.
~Delay future updates until certainty is complete#Not the best answer. Transparent updates can preserve credibility when evidence evolves.
}

::HC-W8-044::In Week 8 (Digital Health and Social Media Communication), in a malaria-control programme, a communication strategy works well for smartphone users but misses people without data access. Which principle needs stronger attention? {
=Equity and accessibility#Correct. Effectiveness should be assessed across groups, including those facing access barriers.
~Message saturation#Not the best answer. Effectiveness should be assessed across groups, including those facing access barriers.
~Brand visibility#Not the best answer. Effectiveness should be assessed across groups, including those facing access barriers.
~Technical complexity#Not the best answer. Effectiveness should be assessed across groups, including those facing access barriers.
}

::HC-W8-045::In Week 8 (Digital Health and Social Media Communication), in a school health programme, a team immediately chooses Instagram before defining the audience or objective. What is the BEST correction? {
=Diagnose the communication problem and audience before selecting a channel#Correct. Channel choice should follow the communication problem, audience and objective.
~Increase posting frequency#Not the best answer. Channel choice should follow the communication problem, audience and objective.
~Use more technical terminology#Not the best answer. Channel choice should follow the communication problem, audience and objective.
~Remove all audience feedback#Not the best answer. Channel choice should follow the communication problem, audience and objective.
}

